": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 1.1977, "filing_name": "JPMorgan Chase & Co 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/19617/000162828026008131/jpm-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 4, "dropped_candidates": 134, "token_estimate": 31097, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "JPMorgan Chase reported net interest income of $95,443 million for fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025 [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0538]. This compares with $92,583 million for fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024, an increase of 3.1% [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0805]. On a managed basis, net interest income was $95,868 million, and net interest income excluding Markets was $92,591 million [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0074]. The 10-K attributes the increase to higher Markets net interest income, higher revolving balances in Card Services, higher wholesale deposit balances, and investment securities activity, largely offset by deposit margin compression and lower rates [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0020].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "JPM", "company": "JPMorgan Chase & Co", "findings": [{"point": "Reported net interest income was $95,443 million for fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025, versus $92,583 million for fiscal 2024 and $89,267 million for fiscal 2023, ended December 31, 2023.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0538"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Managed-basis net interest income was $95,868 million after $425 million of fully taxable-equivalent adjustments; excluding Markets it was $92,591 million, with a net yield of 2.50% on managed average interest-earning assets.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0074"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Management stated that fiscal 2025 NII rose 3% on higher Markets NII, Card Services 